This study details a search for the associated production of Higgs boson pairs ($HH$) using 139 fb$^{-1}$ of proton-proton collision data at a center-of-mass energy of 13 TeV, recorded by the ATLAS detector at the Large Hadron Collider. The analysis targets decays into two photons and associated $W$ or $Z$ boson production, specifically looking for the $Z ightarrow \ell\ell^{\pm}$ and $W ightarrow \ell
u$ decay channels. The observed number of events aligns with background predictions, leading to upper limits on the cross-section times branching ratio of 10.1 fb for the $WZ ightarrow \ell^{+}
u\ell^{+}\ell^{+}$ channel and 10.6 fb for the $WZ ightarrow \ell^{+}
u\ell^{+}\ell^{+}$ channel at the Standard Model level. These findings are interpreted within the context of the Standard Model Higgs framework and the MSSM, yielding lower bounds on the masses of 125.5 GeV and 126.0 GeV, respectively.
